  "summary": "Manual transmission shift linkage (4-speed shift rods and levers on the side of the transmission). Two shift rods run from the floor shifter levers back to two levers on the transmission side cover: rod [6] ends in a threaded swivel [13] locked by two nuts [10] whose pin goes into lever [14] (washer [15] + retainer [4]); rod [5] ends in a clevis [11] locked by a nut [10] and pinned to lever asm [18] with pin [12], spring washer [16] and cotter pin [17]. Each transmission lever is held on its shaft by a bolt [7] with lock washer [8] and flat washer [9]; the rod ends at the shifter are held by spring-clip retainers [4]; bolt [2] with lock washer [1] goes into the transmission case.",
